course: dictionary
lesson: 2129
title: Cook: a verb and a noun
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Cook can be a verb (an action word) or a noun (a naming word). As a verb, to cook means to make food ready to eat by heating it, such as boiling, frying, baking or roasting. «Roll up sleeves and tie back long hair before cooking» is about an action, so cook is a verb there.
explain: Context tells you which meaning you need. In «a cook is a person who prepares food», the word names a person, so it is a noun. Read the words around cook and ask: is this an action or a person?
explain: Food cooks when heat changes it until it is ready to eat. Cooking changes food: eggs go solid and bread browns. «Cashews are sold shelled and cooked» means they have been heated and are ready to eat.
fact: Cook as a verb means to make food ready to eat by heating it.
fact: A cook is a person who prepares food, at home or as a job.
fact: «Cook dinner» means to make dinner by heating the food.
fact: Heat kills germs, so meat and eggs must be cooked all the way through before you eat them.
fact: «Cook up» can mean to invent a story or plan, and «too many cooks spoil the broth» means too many people helping can make a job worse.
exercise: «Roll up sleeves and tie back long hair before cooking.» Is cooking a verb or a noun here? | Noun, a person | Noun, a kitchen tool | Adjective, a describing word | *Verb, an action
exercise: What does «a cook» mean? | *A person who prepares food | A pan used for frying | A cold drink with ice | Someone who is always late
exercise: «Cashews are sold shelled and cooked.» What does cooked mean here? | Made up as a story | Sold in a bag | Hidden inside a shell | *Heated until ready to eat
test: «Heat kills germs, so meat and eggs must be cooked through.» Why must meat be cooked through? | To make it heavier | *To kill germs so it is safe to eat | To make it colder | To change its colour only
test: Dad says, «Too many cooks spoil the broth», when three people try to help with soup. What does he mean? | *Too many people helping can make a job worse | Cooks should never make soup | Cooks must be very tall | Soup is always better with lots of cooks
exam: Which sentence uses cook as a noun? | We cook pasta on Fridays. | *Mum is the best cook in our family. | Cook your eggs for five minutes. | Turn the pan handles in before you cook.
